{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Moses charged, and the elders of Israel.</b> The reason for mentioning the elders of Israel here is that Moses intended by this what our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Berakhot 19b) — that where there is a profanation of HaShem's name one does not show deference to a master, as it is written (Proverbs 21:30): ״אֵין חָכְמָה וְגוֹ׳ לְנֶגֶד ה׳״ (there is no wisdom etc. against YHWH). And this is the meaning of his saying ״וַיְצַו מֹשֶׁה״ — although He stands before them as the master of all Israel, he did so that even the elders would command and admonish concerning the matter, saying ״שָׁמוֹר״ etc. He was precise in saying <b>שָׁמוֹר</b> to signal that regarding this matter, which is a negative commandment (Makkot 13a), it is as they said that one does not show deference to a master — as is known."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:19:14.125206256Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}